[{"category":"section","location":"#Gecko.jl","page":"Home","text":"Documentation for Gecko.jl, a Julia wrapper for the C++ graph ordering library Gecko.","title":"Gecko.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#How-to-use-the-library","page":"Home","text":"using Gecko\n\n# Graph with 4 nodes\ng = GeckoGraph(4)\n\n# Connect to quadrilateral. Insertion must be sorted by the first node index.\nadd_directed_edge!(g, 1, 2)\nadd_directed_edge!(g, 1, 3)\nadd_directed_edge!(g, 2, 1)\nadd_directed_edge!(g, 2, 4)\nadd_directed_edge!(g, 3, 1)\nadd_directed_edge!(g, 3, 4)\nadd_directed_edge!(g, 4, 2)\nadd_directed_edge!(g, 4, 3)\n\n# Optimize ordering\norder!(g)\n\n# We can now access the optimized ordering via\nnew_index(g, 2 #= old_node_index =#)","title":"How to use the library"},{"category":"section","location":"#Citing-Gecko","page":"Home","text":"If you use gecko for scholarly research, please cite the following paper:\n\nPeter Lindstrom The Minimum Edge Product Linear Ordering Problem LLNL technical report LLNL-TR-496076, August 26, 2011.","title":"Citing Gecko"},{"category":"section","location":"#Public-API-Reference","page":"Home","text":"The following functionals are provided.\n\nFunctionalQuasiconvex\nFunctionalHarmonic\nFunctionalGeometric\nFunctionalSMR\nFunctionalArithmetic\nFunctionalRMS\nFunctionalMaximum","title":"Public API Reference"},{"category":"type","location":"#Gecko.GeckoGraph","page":"Home","text":"GeckoGraph([nnodes])\n\nGecko multilevel graph for linear ordering problems.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Gecko.GeckoGraph"},{"category":"function","location":"#Gecko.add_node!","page":"Home","text":"add_node!(graph::GeckoGraph)\n\nAdd a new node to the graph wth index num_nodes + 1.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Gecko.add_node!"},{"category":"function","location":"#Gecko.add_directed_edge!","page":"Home","text":"add_directed_edge!(graph::GeckoGraph, i::Integer, j::Integer)\n\nAdd a new directed edge to the graph, connecting nodes i and j. Insertion must be sorted by the first node index i, i.e. if we insert an edge with i=3, then we cannot add an edge with i=2 afterwards.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Gecko.add_directed_edge!"},{"category":"function","location":"#Gecko.cost","page":"Home","text":"cost(graph::GeckoGraph)\n\nReturn the current cost of the ordered graph.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Gecko.cost"},{"category":"function","location":"#Gecko.num_nodes","page":"Home","text":"num_nodes(graph::GeckoGraph)\n\nThe current number of nodes in the graph.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Gecko.num_nodes"},{"category":"function","location":"#Gecko.num_edges","page":"Home","text":"num_nodes(graph::GeckoGraph)\n\nThe current number of edges in the graph.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Gecko.num_edges"},{"category":"function","location":"#Gecko.order!","page":"Home","text":"order!(graph::GeckoGraph [, params::GraphOrderingParameters])\n\nReorder the graph, using the parameter set in GraphOrderingParameters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Gecko.order!"},{"category":"function","location":"#Gecko.new_index","page":"Home","text":"num_nodes(graph::GeckoGraph, i::Integer)\n\nThe new index of node i after reordering.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Gecko.new_index"},{"category":"type","location":"#Gecko.GraphOrderingParameters","page":"Home","text":"GraphOrderingParameters(;kwargs)\n\nkwargs can be one of the following:\n\nOptimization functional functional = FunctionalGeometric()\nNumber of V cycles iterations = 9\nInitial window size window = 5\nNumber of iterations between window increments period = 2\nRandom number seed seed = 1\n\nFor more details on the parameters please consult the Gecko paper.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Gecko.GraphOrderingParameters"}]
